From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] the immersive-mode cling is readable, and does not dim the page

The first time an application goes fullscreen, the system puts up a panel that
says what happened and how to get out of it. On this device that panel is a
black slab with nothing on it but a chevron and 知道了: the two lines that
carry the whole message are invisible.

AOSP's layout (core/res/res/layout/immersive_mode_cling.xml) paints the panel
in `?android:attr/colorAccent` and writes the title and the description in
`@color/primary_text_default_material_light`, which is #de000000. That works
because an accent colour is a mid-tone: dark body text reads on it, and so
does the white 知道了. Rule 2 of docs/design/eink-ui.md makes the accent black
here -- Material's teal lands on grey level 2 on this panel, which is only
slightly lighter than body text -- so the panel became black and the text with
it. Everything that stayed legible is what AOSP had drawn in white.

Photographed and then read off the device: the panel is [0,0]-[1072,468],
uniformly #000000 apart from the chevron's white circle and the 知道了 in the
corner. `uiautomator dump` has both TextViews present, laid out and on screen
(immersive_cling_title at [0,98][1072,234], immersive_cling_description at
[0,234][1072,299]) -- nothing is clipped or missing, the ink is the same colour
as the paper.

So the panel becomes what every other floating surface in this build already
is: white, with a black line where it meets the page (rule 1, rule 3). The two
TextViews are then left exactly as AOSP wrote them. 知道了 moves from white to
the accent, which is Material's own meaning for it and black here. The chevron
is already tinted with the accent, and its white backing circles simply stop
showing, which leaves a black chevron on white.

The line is a plain View rather than a background drawable with a stroke,
because a new drawable would be a new name in framework-res and every name
there shifts the resource IDs after it (docs/design/eink-ui.md, "数值在哪里定
义"): framework.jar changes, the boot image changes, and every application in
/data has to be compiled again. Changing values inside an existing layout adds
no name. The panel's 24dp of bottom padding moves to the button's margin so
that the line sits on the panel's edge and not 24dp inside it.

The second thing on that screen is the dimming. ClingWindowView fills the
display and paints BGCOLOR = 0x80000000 behind the panel, and with no GPU
(`ActivityManager.isHighEndGfx()` false) it is set at once rather than faded
in. Rule 4 is that nothing dims the page behind it: 50 % black turns white
paper into grey level 2, so putting the cling up and taking it down are two
full-screen 16-level updates, about 463 ms each, and they leave the page
ghosted. The scrim is decoration -- the window is FLAG_NOT_TOUCH_MODAL and not
focusable, so what is behind it stays touchable either way -- and with the
colour transparent only the panel's own rectangle is painted.

